<div class="container">

<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<!-- SECTION 1: PERIODIC TABLE -->
<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<div id="pt">
  <div class="sec-header">
    <div class="sec-icon" style="background:rgba(56,189,248,0.12); color:var(--accent);">⚛️</div>
    <div class="sec-title" style="color:var(--accent)">1. PERIODIC TABLE</div>
    <div class="sec-tag" style="background:rgba(56,189,248,0.1); color:var(--accent); border:1px solid rgba(56,189,248,0.2)">~5 Qs/paper</div>
  </div>

  <div class="grid">
    <!-- Zeff -->
    <div class="card card-b1">
      <div class="card-title" style="color:var(--accent)">⚡ Effective Nuclear Charge (Z*)</div>
      <div class="formula">Z* = Z – σ (shielding constant)</div>
      <ul class="notes">
        <li>Outer shell electrons → <span class="hl hl-r">shielding = 0</span></li>
        <li>Same shell electrons → partial shielding</li>
        <li>Inner shell → full shielding</li>
        <li><b>s & p block</b> L→R: Z* ↑ by 0.65; T→B: Z* constant</li>
        <li><b>d block</b> L→R: Z* ↑ by 0.15; T→B: Z* ↑</li>
        <li><b>f block</b> L→R: Z* constant (Lanthanide Contraction)</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <!-- Atomic Radius -->
    <div class="card card-b1">
      <div class="card-title" style="color:var(--accent)">📏 Atomic Radius Trends</div>
      <div class="formula">r<sub>vdW</sub> &gt; r<sub>metallic</sub> &gt; r<sub>covalent</sub></div>
      <ul class="notes">
        <li><b>Period (L→R):</b> Generally ↓ (Z* ↑)</li>
        <li><b>Group (T→B):</b> Generally ↑ (n ↑)</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="alert alert-warn">
        <div class="alert-icon">⚠️</div>
        <div><b>Exceptions Grp 13:</b> B &lt; Al &gt; Ga &lt; In &lt; Tl (Lanthanide contraction effect)<br>
        <b>Grp 14:</b> C &lt; Si &lt; Ge &lt; Sn ≈ Pb</div>
      </div>
      <ul class="notes">
        <li><b>d-block T→B:</b> Grp 4-12: 3d &lt; 4d ≈ 5d (Lanthanide contraction)</li>
        <li><b>f-block Metallic:</b> Eu &gt; Ce &gt; Pr... &gt; Lu</li>
        <li><b>f-block Ionic M³⁺:</b> Ce &gt; Pr... &gt; Lu</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <!-- Ionisation Energy -->
    <div class="card card-b1">
      <div class="card-title" style="color:var(--accent)">⚡ Ionisation Energy (IE)</div>
      <div class="formula">X(g) → X⁺(g) + e⁻ [always +ve, endothermic]</div>
      <ul class="notes">
        <li>IE₁ &lt; IE₂ &lt; IE₃ (successive IE always ↑)</li>
        <li><b>L→R:</b> Generally ↑ (Z* ↑)</li>
        <li><b>T→B:</b> Generally ↓ (size ↑)</li>
        <li><span class="hl hl-g">He = highest IE; Cs = lowest IE</span></li>
      </ul>
      <div class="alert alert-warn">
        <div class="alert-icon">⚠️</div>
        <div><b>Dip at B vs Be:</b> Be(2s²) &gt; B(2p¹) due to penetration<br>
        <b>Dip at O vs N:</b> N(2p³ half-filled) &gt; O(2p⁴) due to stability<br>
        <b>Grp 13 T→B:</b> B &gt; Tl &gt; Ga &gt; Al &gt; In</div>
      </div>
      <div class="memory-box">
        <div class="mem-title">⚡ Jump in successive IE → tells valence electrons</div>
        <p>ΔIE ≥ 16 eV → lower OS stable | ΔIE ≤ 11 eV → higher OS stable</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Electron Affinity -->
    <div class="card card-b1">
      <div class="card-title" style="color:var(--accent)">📥 Electron Affinity (EA)</div>
      <div class="formula">ΔH_eg ≈ −EA | X(g) + e⁻ → X⁻(g)</div>
      <ul class="notes">
        <li>1st EA mostly <b>exothermic</b> (except Be, Mg, N, Noble gases)</li>
        <li>2nd EA always <b>endothermic</b> (inter-electron repulsion)</li>
        <li><b>L→R:</b> Generally ↑ | <b>T→B:</b> Generally ↓</li>
        <li><span class="hl hl-y">Cl &gt; F</span> (F has small size, high e⁻ repulsion)</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="alert alert-warn">
        <div class="alert-icon">⚠️</div>
        <div><b>Grp 17:</b> F &lt; Cl &gt; Br &gt; I<br>
        <b>Grp 16:</b> O &lt; S &gt; Se &gt; Te<br>
        Halogens have highest EA among all groups</div>
      </div>
      <ul class="notes">
        <li>EA₁ of neutral atom = IE₁ of its anion</li>
        <li>IE₁ of neutral atom &gt; EA₁ of neutral atom</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <!-- Electronegativity -->
    <div class="card card-b1">
      <div class="card-title" style="color:var(--accent)">🧲 Electronegativity (EN)</div>
      <div class="formula">% Ionic character = 16(ΔEN) + 3.5(ΔEN)²</div>
      <div class="formula">d(A-B) = rA + rB – 0.09(ΔEN) [Schomaker-Stevenson]</div>
      <ul class="notes">
        <li><span class="hl hl-g">F = 4.0 (highest) | Cs = 0.7 (lowest)</span></li>
        <li><b>L→R:</b> ↑ | <b>T→B:</b> ↓</li>
        <li>OS ↑ → EN of atom ↑ (Mn &lt; Mn²⁺ &lt; Mn⁷⁺)</li>
        <li>% s-character ↑ → EN ↑ (sp³ &lt; sp² &lt; sp)</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="alert alert-tip">
        <div class="alert-icon">💡</div>
        <div>Acid strength of hydra-acids: L→R ↑ EN; T→B ↑ Size<br>
        Acid strength of oxyacids: ↑ OS of same central atom → ↑ acid strength</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Oxides -->
    <div class="card card-b1">
      <div class="card-title" style="color:var(--accent)">🔥 Types of Oxides</div>
      <ul class="notes">
        <li><span class="hl hl-r">Acidic:</span> CO₂, N₂O₅, SO₃, B₂O₃, P₄O₁₀</li>
        <li><span class="hl hl-g">Basic:</span> Li₂O, Na₂O, MgO, CaO, SrO</li>
        <li><span class="hl hl-b">Neutral:</span> CO, N₂O, NO, H₂O</li>
        <li><span class="hl hl-p">Amphoteric:</span> ZnO, BeO, Al₂O₃, Ga₂O₃, MnO₂, SnO, Cr₂O₃, V₂O₅, PbO, PbO₂</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="alert alert-warn">
        <div class="alert-icon">⚠️</div>
        <div>Acidic nature of oxides: Acidic &gt; Amphoteric &gt; Basic<br>
        Acidic nature ∝ OS of element (same element)</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Ionic Radius Important Orders -->
