  <div class="grid" style="margin-top:14px">
    <!-- VSEPR -->
    <div class="card card-b2">
      <div class="card-title" style="color:var(--accent2)">🔄 VSEPR Rules</div>
      <ul class="notes">
        <li><b>Repulsion order:</b> LP-LP &gt; LP-SB &gt; SB-SB</li>
        <li>Also: DB-DB &gt; DB-SB &gt; SB-SB</li>
        <li>LP compresses adjacent bond angles by ~2.5° each</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="alert alert-tip">
        <div class="alert-icon">💡</div>
        <div><b>Bent's Rule:</b> LP occupies positions of highest p-character (equatorial in sp³d). More EN atoms → axial positions in sp³d</div>
      </div>
      <div class="alert alert-warn">
        <div class="alert-icon">⚠️</div>
        <div><b>Drago's Rule:</b> 3rd period+ central atom with LP + SA of EN &lt; 3 → no hybridisation → bond angle ≈ 90°<br>
        PH₃, H₂S, AsH₃, H₂Se etc.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Bond Parameters -->
    <div class="card card-b2">
      <div class="card-title" style="color:var(--accent2)">📐 Bond Parameters</div>
      <ul class="notes">
        <li><b>Bond Order ↑ → BE ↑, BL ↓</b></li>
        <li><b>% s-character:</b> sp(50%) &gt; sp²(33%) &gt; sp³(25%)</li>
        <li><b>Bond Length:</b> sp &lt; sp² &lt; sp³</li>
        <li><b>2nd period single bonds:</b> BE ∝ 1/No. of lone pairs on bonded atoms</li>
        <li><span class="hl hl-r">F-F &lt; Cl-Cl</span> (F has more LP repulsion)</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="alert alert-tip">
        <div class="alert-icon">💡</div>
        <div><b>Bond Angle order:</b><br>
        NH₃ &gt; PH₃ &gt; AsH₃ &gt; SbH₃<br>
        H₂O &gt; H₂S &gt; H₂Se &gt; H₂Te<br>
        NF₃ &lt; NH₃ (F withdraws e⁻ → compresses)</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Dipole Moment -->
    <div class="card card-b2">
      <div class="card-title" style="color:var(--accent2)">🧲 Dipole Moment (μ)</div>
      <div class="formula2">μ = q × d (Debye) | 1D = 3.33×10⁻³⁰ C·m</div>
      <ul class="notes">
        <li>Direction: less EN → more EN atom (δ+ → δ−)</li>
        <li>LP moment: always away from nucleus</li>
        <li>Regular (symmetrical) structures → μ = 0 (non-polar)</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="alert alert-warn">
        <div class="alert-icon">⚠️</div>
        <div><b>Key orders:</b><br>
        NH₃ &gt; NF₃ (LP & bond moments cancel in NF₃)<br>
        H₂O &gt; H₂O₂<br>
        CHCl₃ &gt; CH₂Cl₂ &gt; CH₃Cl &gt; CCl₄ = CH₄ = 0<br>
        H₂O &gt; HF &gt; NH₃</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- MOT -->
    <div class="card card-b2">
      <div class="card-title" style="color:var(--accent2)">🌀 MOT – Bond Orders</div>
      <div class="formula2">BO = (Nb − Na) / 2</div>
      <div class="tbl-wrap">
