  </div>

  <!-- Hydrogen Bond -->
  <div class="card card-b2" style="margin-top:14px">
    <div class="card-title" style="color:var(--accent2)">💧 Hydrogen Bond & van der Waals Forces</div>
    <div class="two-col">
      <div>
        <ul class="notes">
          <li>X−H···Y (X, Y = F, O, N)</li>
          <li><b>Intermolecular H-bond:</b> ↑ BP, MP, viscosity, surface tension, enthalpy of vaporisation; ↓ vapour pressure</li>
          <li><b>Intramolecular H-bond:</b> forms chelate ring (5 or 6 membered); ↑ volatile nature; ↓ BP vs intermolecular</li>
          <li>o-nitrophenol (intra) → lower BP than p-nitrophenol (inter)</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div>
        <ul class="notes">
          <li><b>H-bond strength order:</b> HF···HF &gt; H₂O···H₂O &gt; NH₃···NH₃</li>
          <li><b>VWF ∝</b> Size, Mol. mass, Surface area</li>
          <li>London forces: non-polar + non-polar</li>
          <li>ICl &gt; Br₂ (despite same electrons – ICl has dipole)</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="alert alert-imp">
          <div class="alert-icon">🔴</div>
          <div>BP: HF &lt; H₂O &gt; H₂S (H₂O has strong H-bond network)</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Fajan's Rule -->
  <div class="card card-b2" style="margin-top:14px">
    <div class="card-title" style="color:var(--accent2)">⚡ Fajan's Rule – Polarisation</div>
    <div class="two-col">
      <div>
        <ul class="notes">
          <li><b>Polarising Power (cation) ↑ if:</b> Charge ↑, Size ↓, Pseudo-inert gas &gt; Inert pair &gt; Inert gas config</li>
          <li><b>Polarisability (anion) ↑ if:</b> Charge ↑ (−ve), Size ↑</li>
          <li>High polarisation → more covalent character</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div class="formula2">Pseudo-inert gas (18e⁻) &gt; Inert pair (18+2) &gt; Inert gas (8e⁻)</div>
        <ul class="notes">
          <li>NaF &lt; MgF₂ &lt; AlF₃ (MP increases as covalent character ↑)</li>
          <li>NaCl &gt; MgCl₂ &gt; AlCl₃ (MP decreases)</li>
          <li>Covalent solid &gt; Ionic solid &gt; Molecular solid (MP)</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

