          <div class="flow-row">
            <div class="flow-ion">I⁻</div>
            <div class="flow-reagent">Conc. H₂SO₄</div>
            <div class="flow-obs">I₂ (violet) | Starch → blue-black | Layer test</div>
          </div>
          <div class="flow-row">
            <div class="flow-ion">NO₃⁻</div>
            <div class="flow-reagent">Conc. H₂SO₄ + Cu</div>
            <div class="flow-obs">NO₂ (reddish brown) | Brown Ring test (same as NO₂⁻)</div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="alert alert-warn">
          <div class="alert-icon">⚠️</div>
          <div><b>Chromyl chloride test fails for:</b> AgCl, Cu₂Cl₂, CCl₄, CHCl₃, HgCl₂, Hg₂Cl₂, PbCl₂, PbCl₄</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Class B Anions -->
  <div class="card card-b6" style="margin-top:14px">
    <div class="card-title" style="color:var(--accent6)">Class B Anions (No volatile product with H₂SO₄)</div>
    <div class="two-col">
      <div>
        <div class="trend-title">Sub-group I (By ppt)</div>
        <div class="flow-group">
          <div class="flow-row"><div class="flow-ion">SO₄²⁻</div><div class="flow-reagent">BaCl₂ + HCl</div><div class="flow-obs">White ppt BaSO₄ (insoluble in HCl)</div></div>
          <div class="flow-row"><div class="flow-ion">PO₄³⁻</div><div class="flow-reagent">Amm. Molybdate</div><div class="flow-obs">Yellow ppt (ammonium phosphomolybdate)</div></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div class="trend-title">Sub-group II (Redox tests)</div>
        <div class="flow-group">
          <div class="flow-row"><div class="flow-ion">Cr₂O₇²⁻</div><div class="flow-reagent">Acidic medium</div><div class="flow-obs">Orange → Green when reduced</div></div>
          <div class="flow-row"><div class="flow-ion">MnO₄⁻</div><div class="flow-reagent">Reducing agent</div><div class="flow-obs">Purple → colourless/brown</div></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Cation Groups -->
  <div class="card card-b6" style="margin-top:14px">
    <div class="card-title" style="color:var(--accent6)">⚗️ Cation Groups – Systematic Analysis</div>
    <div class="tbl-wrap">
      <table>
        <tr><th>Group</th><th>Cations</th><th>Reagent</th><th>Precipitate</th><th>Colour</th></tr>
        <tr><td>0</td><td>NH₄⁺</td><td>NaOH (warm)</td><td>NH₃ gas (smell + moist litmus)</td><td>–</td></tr>
        <tr><td>I</td><td>Ag⁺, Hg₂²⁺, Pb²⁺</td><td>dil. HCl</td><td>AgCl, Hg₂Cl₂, PbCl₂</td><td>White</td></tr>
        <tr><td>IIA</td><td>Pb²⁺, Cu²⁺, Bi³⁺, Hg²⁺, Cd²⁺</td><td>H₂S/H⁺</td><td>PbS, CuS, Bi₂S₃, HgS, CdS</td><td>Black/Yellow(Cd)</td></tr>
        <tr><td>IIB</td><td>As³⁺/⁵⁺, Sb³⁺/⁵⁺, Sn²⁺/⁴⁺</td><td>H₂S/H⁺</td><td>As₂S₃/₅, Sb₂S₃/₅, SnS/SnS₂</td><td>Yellow/Orange</td></tr>
        <tr><td>III</td><td>Fe³⁺, Cr³⁺, Al³⁺</td><td>NH₄Cl + NH₄OH</td><td>Fe(OH)₃, Cr(OH)₃, Al(OH)₃</td><td>Brown/Green/White</td></tr>
        <tr><td>IV</td><td>Ni²⁺, Co²⁺, Mn²⁺, Zn²⁺</td><td>H₂S/OH⁻</td><td>NiS, CoS, MnS, ZnS</td><td>Black/Pink/Buff/White</td></tr>
        <tr><td>V</td><td>Ba²⁺, Sr²⁺, Ca²⁺</td><td>(NH₄)₂CO₃ + NH₄OH</td><td>BaCO₃, SrCO₃, CaCO₃</td><td>White</td></tr>
        <tr><td>VI</td><td>Na⁺, K⁺, Mg²⁺</td><td>Flame test / specific</td><td>–</td><td>Yellow/Lilac/–</td></tr>
      </table>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Specific Tests -->
  <div class="card card-b6" style="margin-top:14px">
    <div class="card-title" style="color:var(--accent6)">🎯 Specific Confirmatory Tests (High Yield)</div>
    <div class="grid-3">
      <div>
        <div class="trend-title">Fe³⁺</div>
        <div class="rxn">K₄[Fe(CN)₆] → Fe₄[Fe(CN)₆]₃ (Prussian Blue)<br>SCN⁻ → Fe(SCN)₃ (Blood Red)</div>
        <div class="trend-title">Fe²⁺</div>
        <div class="rxn">K₃[Fe(CN)₆] → Fe₃[Fe(CN)₆]₂ (Turnbull's Blue)<br>DMG → no reaction</div>
        <div class="trend-title">Cu²⁺</div>
        <div class="rxn">NH₄OH (excess) → [Cu(NH₃)₄]²⁺ (deep blue)<br>K₄[Fe(CN)₆] → Cu₂[Fe(CN)₆]↓ (chocolate)</div>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div class="trend-title">Ni²⁺</div>
        <div class="rxn">DMG (dmg⁻¹) + NH₄OH → [Ni(dmg)₂] (rosy red ppt)</div>
        <div class="trend-title">Al³⁺</div>
        <div class="rxn">Excess NaOH → Na[Al(OH)₄] (soluble)<br>Lake test → Al(OH)₃ + litmus → blue floating ppt</div>
        <div class="trend-title">Zn²⁺</div>
        <div class="rxn">NaOH: Zn(OH)₂ → excess NaOH → Na₂[Zn(OH)₄]<br>K₄[Fe(CN)₆] → Zn₂[Fe(CN)₆]↓ (white)</div>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div class="trend-title">Ba²⁺ vs Ca²⁺</div>
        <div class="rxn">Ba²⁺: Flame → Apple green | K₂CrO₄ → BaCrO₄ (yellow, insoluble in CH₃COOH)<br>Ca²⁺: Flame → Brick red | (NH₄)₂C₂O₄ → CaC₂O₄ (white)</div>
        <div class="trend-title">NH₄⁺</div>
        <div class="rxn">NaOH (warm) → NH₃↑<br>Nessler's K₂[HgI₄]+KOH → brown ppt</div>
        <div class="trend-title">Pb²⁺</div>
        <div class="rxn">Na₂SO₄ → PbSO₄↓ (white)<br>Na₂CrO₄ → PbCrO₄↓ (yellow)</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Dry Tests -->
  <div class="card card-b6" style="margin-top:14px">
    <div class="card-title" style="color:var(--accent6)">🔥 Dry Tests – Flame & Borax Bead</div>
    <div class="two-col">
      <div>
        <div class="trend-title">Flame Test Colours</div>
        <div class="tbl-wrap">
          <table>
            <tr><th>Metal</th><th>Flame Colour</th></tr>
            <tr><td>Li</td><td>Crimson Red</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Na</td><td>Golden Yellow</td></tr>
            <tr><td>K</td><td>Lilac/Violet</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Rb</td><td>Red-Violet</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Cs</td><td>Blue</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Ca</td><td>Brick Red</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Sr</td><td>Crimson Red</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Ba</td><td>Apple Green</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Cu²⁺</td><td>Blue-Green</td></tr>
            <tr><td>BO₃³⁻</td><td>Green Edge</td></tr>
          </table>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div class="trend-title">Borax Bead Test</div>
        <div class="tbl-wrap">
          <table>
            <tr><th>Ion</th><th>Oxidising (Cold)</th><th>Reducing (Hot)</th></tr>
            <tr><td>Cu²⁺</td><td>Blue</td><td>Red opaque (Cu)</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Co²⁺</td><td>Blue</td><td>Blue</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Ni²⁺</td><td>Brown</td><td>–</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Cr³⁺</td><td>Green</td><td>–</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Mn²⁺</td><td>Pink/violet</td><td>–</td></tr>
          </table>
        </div>
        <div class="trend-title" style="margin-top:10px">Charcoal Cavity Test</div>
        <ul class="notes">
          <li>White (cold) + Yellow (hot) → Zn²⁺</li>
          <li>Brown → Cd²⁺</li>
          <li>White + Garlic smell → As³⁺</li>
          <li>Co(NO₃)₂: Rinmann's Green = Zn²⁺; Thenard's Blue = Al³⁺; Pink = Mg²⁺</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

